{"archetypes":[{"name":"runtime-compat","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff lowers the runtime Python floor to 3.11 across code, docs, CI, and tooling pins, which needs cross-file consistency and syntax/API scrutiny.","prompt_body":"Investigate whether every changed Python runtime floor, lint/type target, CI matrix entry, and shell guard consistently supports Python 3.11 without accidentally relying on 3.12-only syntax or tooling behavior. Pay special attention to python/pyproject.toml, python/ruff.toml, python/pyrightconfig.json, python/.pylintrc, workflow setup-python matrices, and runtime probes in shell scripts. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"gh-cli-contract","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The PR creation path depends on real gh CLI stdout behavior and fallback recovery after removing unsupported JSON flags.","prompt_body":"Investigate the gh pr create integration contract after removing --json, including argv construction, stdout URL recovery, branch lookup lag, and error mapping through ShipError. Check whether the new fixture or real-CLI-style tests actually protect against reintroducing unsupported gh flags and whether successful creation can still resolve the PR robustly. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"merge-head-sync","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The merge path changes PR head OID synchronization and removes a pre-merge flush, both of which affect CI convergence and merge safety.","prompt_body":"Investigate the merge flow around force-push recovery, PR head OID polling, retry caps, and removal of pre-merge flush behavior. Look for cases where the code could merge the wrong head, loop longer than intended, return an incorrect merge result, or diverge from the bash parity contract. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"runlog-porcelain","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The volatile-only run-log skip path manipulates git state and must fail closed without losing substantive logs or leaving dirty porcelain.","prompt_body":"Investigate the run-log flush changes that classify refresh sidecars as volatile-only, restore or clean them, and assert repo-wide porcelain is empty before treating the flush as a no-op. Check allowlist boundaries, staged versus unstaged cleanup, untracked handling, failure propagation, and whether canonical token or timing reports can still commit substantive changes. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"stream-contract","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The Python ship driver now emits progress breadcrumbs while promising stdout remains a single JSON object.","prompt_body":"Investigate the stdout and stderr contract for the Python ship path and CI polling breadcrumbs. Verify that progress output is consistently sent only to stderr, JSON result emission remains isolated on stdout, and tests cover both normal and error paths without depending on brittle timing text. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"shell-sete","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The sourced routing parser fix is specifically about set -e interactions that are easy to miss in shell short-circuit code.","prompt_body":"Investigate the parse-bootstrap routing envelope shell changes under set -euo pipefail, especially duplicate file-first and stdout-fallback keys, preserve-coder behavior, and helper return statuses. Check whether the new harness accurately reproduces the failure mode and whether Makefile registration is complete without duplicate or misplaced targets causing maintenance drift. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
